<h2 id="colors">Colors</h2>
{% include "partials/design-tokens.njk" %}
{% markdown %}
Use `--kh-cart-paper`, `--kh-cart-ink`, `--kh-cart-blue`, `--kh-cart-yellow`, `--kh-cart-red` and `--kh-cart-green`. The swatches above consume the live tokens. Yellow and red are large decorative accents. Use white/cobalt, white/green, ink/paper and cobalt/paper for text. Muted text uses `--kh-ink-muted` (`#5b5e5a`).

The [design guide palette](/style-guide/design/#palette) records contrast and colour roles. Existing aliases keep earlier components in step: `--kh-ground` maps to paper; `--kh-color--blue` and `--kh-color--apparatus` map to cobalt; rules use neutral ink. `--kh-panel-bg` is a slightly lighter paper, `#fffdf5`. Visited reading links retain `--kh-color--visited` (`#563d82`).
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="typography">Typography</h2>
<p class="kh-reference-display">Make it make sense.</p>
{% markdown %}
Anton 400 is the display voice. IBM Plex Sans 400/600 is the reading and interface voice; Plex Mono 400 is for code, dates and reference metadata. All are self-hosted. Authored copy remains sentence case; display uppercase is CSS.

Page titles are fluid, up to 4.5rem on standard pages. Utility and photo titles are smaller; article and homepage compositions have their own scales. Long-form reading uses 18px and about 62ch, reducing to 17px on small screens. Avoid fixed widths on text.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<p class="kh-reference-display">An expressive display line</p>
<p>Reading text in IBM Plex Sans. <strong>Emphasis uses the real semibold.</strong> <em>Italic uses the real italic face.</em></p>
<p class="kh-meta">24 Oct 2026 / metadata in Plex Mono</p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="datasheet">Shared structure</h2>
<span id="datasheet-register" aria-hidden="true"></span>
{% markdown %}
The original datasheet class names remain for stable markup. Their current styling belongs to the cartridge system: a plain section name, cobalt structural rule, open lists and lightly separated panels. Decorative section numbers have been removed from index templates. Stable project references and ordered instructions still carry real numbers.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-section-head"><h3>Recent writing</h3><span class="kh-meta">Newest first</span></div>
<div class="kh-panel"><div class="kh-panel__row"><div class="kh-panel__cell"><span class="kh-panel__label">Place</span>Bonn, Germany</div><div class="kh-panel__cell"><span class="kh-panel__label">Practice</span>Platforms, content and audiences</div></div></div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="micro-copy">Labels and micro-copy</h2>
{% markdown %}
Use one name per destination, sentence-case labels, and descriptions that add information rather than repeat the heading. The [interface vocabulary](/style-guide/editorial/#interface-vocabulary) is the naming reference.

`.kh-cartridge-kicker`, `.kh-meta` and `.kh-panel__label` are supporting labels. They must remain readable without hover. Put an explanation next to a data mark when its meaning would otherwise depend on a tooltip. Preserve proper names and acronyms; do not author all-caps text just because its display style is uppercase.
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="buttons">Buttons</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<a class="kh-button" href="/work/">Explore the work</a>
<button class="kh-button" type="button">Example action</button>
<p><a href="/all/">Ordinary navigation stays a link ↗</a></p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Buttons are cobalt with white text, square corners and a minimum 44px target. Hover uses ink; keyboard focus remains visible. Use a button for an action and an anchor with a real destination for navigation. A colour or tilt is not a substitute for link affordance.</p>

<h2 id="badges-labels">Badges and labels</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<p><span class="kh-label">Design systems</span> <span class="kh-label">CSS</span></p>
<p class="kh-meta">Supporting metadata, not a second headline</p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Subjects are labels; dates and reference IDs are metadata. Content-type labels explain the kind of entry. Keep real type names such as “Digesting” and “Impact story”; avoid invented abbreviations.</p>

<h2 id="summary-cards">Entry lists</h2>
{% markdown %}
Wrap the shared `partials/post-summary.njk` in `.kh-datasheet-list`. It supplies the date/body/media wrappers and handles notes, digests and photographs. At desktop widths the list aligns dates, text and figures. On mobile the layout stacks or pairs text and image as space permits. Empty media cells do not get placeholders.

The homepage reverses the list inside `.kh-cartridge-writing`. Dates are yellow, text is white and the blue field is structural. Other lists use ink and cobalt on paper. Project cards use `.kh-work-cards` and `.kh-work-card` on the [work page](/work/), with an upright project image and an actual title.
{% endmarkdown %}
<div class="kh-reference-demo" data-pagefind-ignore><div class="kh-datasheet-list">{% set post = collections.allContent[0] %}{% include "partials/post-summary.njk" %}</div></div>

<h2 id="note-boxes">Note boxes</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<aside class="kh-note-box"><span class="kh-note-box__label">Update</span>A short piece of context that changes how the surrounding text should be read.</aside>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Use a note for context, a correction or a concise summary. Avoid boxing ordinary paragraphs. The left cobalt rule and lighter surface provide emphasis without another display face.</p>

<h2 id="margin-notes">Margin notes and pull-quotes</h2>
{% markdown %}
The `marginnote` shortcode places an aside beside the reading column when room allows and returns it to the flow on small screens. Do not put essential instructions exclusively in a margin. A pull-quote is a selected sentence from the piece, not a replacement for the opening argument. See the [editorial guide](/style-guide/editorial/) for content rules.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<aside class="kh-marginnote"><p>Supporting detail that belongs near this passage.</p></aside>
<p>The main argument remains readable on its own.</p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="content-boxes">Content boxes</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-box"><h3 class="kh-box__heading">A related resource</h3><p class="kh-box__text">A compact grouping of content with a reason to sit together.</p><a href="/garage/">Explore the garage</a></div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="details">Collapsible details</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<details><summary>More implementation detail</summary><p>The content remains native HTML and is usable without JavaScript.</p></details>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>The article contents uses <code>.kh-cartridge-contents</code> around a native details/summary pair, with its navigation inside. Keep the summary descriptive. Do not replace it with a scripted div.</p>

<h2 id="blockquotes">Blockquotes</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<blockquote><p>A quotation is evidence or an outside voice. Give it a source.</p></blockquote>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Ordinary quotes use the reading typeface. The featured quote class remains available for a short, intentional statement, rather than a repeated decoration on every section.</p>

<h2 id="code">Code</h2>
{% markdown %}
Use fenced Markdown for code, with a language identifier. Code uses Plex Mono and a distinct reading surface. Long lines scroll inside their block; the page must not scroll sideways. Inline code may wrap when it would otherwise overflow.

The `codeAndDemo` paired shortcode renders escaped source and the live HTML below it, as in this reference. Its demo becomes real page content: give controls unique IDs and harmless actions. Do not include unsafe sample scripts or live feedback endpoints merely to demonstrate a visual state.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<p>A small live example with <code>inline code</code>.</p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="figures">Figures and images</h2>
{% markdown %}
Put source files in `src/site/images/blog/`; entry frontmatter uses `/blog/filename.ext`. The hero image and the social card are separate mechanisms. Provide descriptive alt text, a useful caption and the correct credit. Ken’s photos use `credit: "Own work."` with location context in the caption.

The image transform can produce a `<picture>` wrapper. In grids and flex layouts, target that direct child as well as the image. Use the original colours of photographs, diagrams and project screenshots. A wide image may break the reading measure, but it must not break the viewport.

The live feedback counter is a remote image and must retain `eleventy:ignore`. A raster still pointing to `/images/` in production, or a `/.11ty/image/` URL in production HTML, is a failed transform; the build checks catch both cases.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<figure class="kh-figure"><img src="/images/cartridge-marks.svg" alt="Blue and red angular lines, a black circle, and two green strokes." width="130" height="130" loading="lazy" eleventy:ignore><figcaption class="kh-figure__caption">Original vector marks used on the cover.</figcaption></figure>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="tables">Tables</h2>
{% markdown %}
Use tables for records that readers compare. `.kh-table--spec` supplies the current cobalt header and neutral rules. `.kh-table-scroll` contains a wide table; `.kh-table--stack` changes suitable record tables into cards below the medium breakpoint. Supply `scope="col"` and meaningful `data-label` values for stacked metadata.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-table-scroll"><table class="kh-table--spec"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Organization</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Shared design system</td><td>2026</td><td>UNDRR</td></tr><tr><td>Visual Framework</td><td>2019</td><td>EMBL</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="forms">Forms</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<form action="/search/" method="get"><label class="kh-form__label" for="guide-search">Search the site</label><input class="kh-form__input" id="guide-search" name="search_query" type="search" placeholder="Try design systems"><button class="kh-button" type="submit">Search</button></form>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Inputs have a real label, a strong neutral boundary and at least 48px height. Placeholder text supports the label rather than replacing it. Native controls, document order and keyboard focus remain the foundation.</p>

<h2 id="search-mode-toggle">Search mode toggle</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<fieldset class="kh-search-mode"><legend>Control preview</legend><label class="kh-search-mode__option"><input type="radio" name="guide-mode" checked>Keyword</label><label class="kh-search-mode__option"><input type="radio" name="guide-mode">Meaning</label></fieldset>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Selected modes use white on cobalt. The actual search page keeps its radio state, keyboard behaviour and URL parameters in sync. This example shows the control styling; use <a href="/search/">Search</a> for working queries.</p>

<h2 id="semantic-search">Semantic search</h2>
<p>The semantic conversation uses the same form and reading primitives as keyword search. Keep loading, error and empty states readable. Model loading, request handling and result generation belong to the existing search implementation; visual changes should not introduce another data path.</p>

<h2 id="metrics">Metrics and data marks</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-metrics-grid"><div class="kh-metric"><span class="kh-metric__number">20+</span><span class="kh-metric__label">Years of work</span></div><div class="kh-metric"><span class="kh-metric__number">5</span><span class="kh-metric__label">Countries</span></div></div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Counts use real data and a visible explanation. Dates, entry kinds, topic tallies, length gauges and similarity scores have different meanings: preserve their labels. Data visualisations keep readable keys and non-colour cues. Use tabular numbers for values that update.</p>

<h2 id="layout">Layout</h2>
{% markdown %}
The shell is capped at 76rem with 2rem desktop gutters and 1rem mobile gutters. The medium breakpoint is 846px. Reading is constrained independently, normally around 62ch. A heading and its introduction start on the same axis; date rails are reserved for lists.

- `.kh-grid` and `.kh-grid__col-3` remain general grid utilities.
- `.kh-grid-stylized` supports label/content layouts. An empty leading placeholder collapses in the current system; do not use an empty column to indent a whole page.
- `.kh-cluster` is plain wrapping flex with a gap and zero child margins. Keep it that way.
- `.kh-stack` retains the established vertical-flow utilities.
- `.kh-bleed-out` is for deliberate wide figures; verify its width at mobile and desktop sizes.
- `.kh-story` and `.kh-scrolly` retain their own wide/reading tracks for interactive pieces.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-cluster"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a><a href="/work/">Work</a><a href="/photos/">Photos</a></div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h2 id="pager">Pager</h2>
<p>The shared pager keeps newer/older destinations and numbered pages as real links. Its accessible label should name the collection. Current-page state belongs only on the current page, while a section underline can identify the parent destination.</p>

<h2 id="spacing">Spacing</h2>
<p>Prefer the component’s layout and gap to extra margins on each child. The existing spacing utilities remain available; <code>kh-u-margin__top--*</code> and <code>kh-u-padding__top--*</code> should express a deliberate section break. Avoid layering them with a second manual offset.</p>

<h2 id="font-variations">Font assets</h2>
{% markdown %}
| Face | Weight | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Anton | 400 | Display headings, self-hosted Latin WOFF2, about 15 KB |
| IBM Plex Sans | 400, 400 italic, 600 | Body and interface |
| IBM Plex Mono | 400 | Code and metadata |
| Recursive Note | 400 | Retained optional personal-note treatment |

The fonts are static assets. Do not use variable-font axis settings on Plex or Anton. A request for 900 does not create a heavier Anton. Keep archived Recursive and Datatype files: posts document and use them. See [font source notes](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/blob/main/docs/FONTS.md).
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="video">Video</h2>
<p>Use the existing responsive video wrapper and a descriptive iframe title. A third-party embed should earn its loading cost; a link is often enough for a reference clip. Keep captions and surrounding explanation useful.</p>

<h2 id="feedback-toast">Feedback</h2>
<p>The feedback partial keeps a real service link and live SVG counter. Do not transform the counter at build time. The confirmation state is supporting UI, not a new page heading. This reference does not submit fake feedback to demonstrate the component.</p>

<h2 id="dappled-light">Earlier visual treatments</h2>
<p>The graph paper, full-site light effect and ruled numbered mastheads are retired from the shared shell. The <a href="/posts/sunlit-dappled-light-effect/">lighting article</a> and <a href="/posts/20250904-switching-to-recursive/">font history</a> preserve the experiments. The <a href="/design-lab/megadrive/">proposal board</a> preserves the design directions. Retaining an archive does not make every archived treatment a current default. Social-sharing cards use the current palette and type in their own fixed-size, noindex document.</p>

<p>Decorative backgrounds use near-white paper, angled colour fields and small sawtooth edges. The writing-field edge and role ribbon use <code>cartridge-edge.svg</code> as a repeated mask; <code>cartridge-pattern.svg</code> supplies sparse cover marks. Patterns belong in margins and section boundaries, with upright content and enough clear space for focus rings.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
{% markdown %}
- Keep a single primary page heading and a useful heading order.
- Use real links, buttons, labels, disclosures and inputs. Primary targets are at least 44px.
- Maintain visible focus against the active surface and readable contrast in every state. Shared controls use an ink outline and white inner ring; check both light and dark surfaces.
- At 200% text sizing, headings and ribbons must reflow without clipping their content.
- Do not rely on hover, colour or motion alone to explain data or controls.
- Keep the CSS checkbox in the DOM. Every custom stylesheet rule is scoped beneath `body:has(#kh-css-toggle:checked)`.
- Honour reduced motion and preserve the no-JavaScript reading path of stories.
- Keep alt text, captions, credits and print output useful.

The skip link, CSS toggle and native disclosures are functional parts of the site. Inspect them at a keyboard, not just in a screenshot.
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="utilities">Utilities and implementation</h2>
{% markdown %}
Layout frontmatter supplies `cartridgeTheme`: `page`, `home`, `article`, `note`, `story`, `photo`, `profile` or `utility`. The base layout supplies the body class and font preload. Avoid repeating the flag in every post when its layout already establishes it.

`_kh-cartridge.scss` owns the palette, shell and cover/article composition. `_kh-cartridge-system.scss` adapts shared components and page families. Older class names remain stable to avoid rewriting archived post markup.

Use `data-pagefind-ignore` for repeated chrome and other entries’ titles. Use `noindex` for non-destinations and `kens_status: draft` for reviewable unpublished posts. Do not replace those shared mechanisms with path lists.

Production checks: `yarn build`, `yarn lint:css`, `yarn lint:links`, `yarn lint:images`, and `yarn lint:overflow`. Check transformed image output, horizontal overflow, 200% text sizing, keyboard focus on light and dark surfaces, search, disclosures, CSS-off mode and representative long-form and interactive pages. Check social-image alt metadata against the card itself, independently of the hero photograph.
{% endmarkdown %}
